.TH _PRINTF 3 "March 2025" "Custom Printf" "User Manual"

.SH NAME
_printf - custom implementation of the printf function

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"

.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B _printf
function is a custom implementation of the standard printf function. It formats and prints output according to the specified format string and arguments.

The function processes the
.I format
string and replaces format specifiers with corresponding values from the variable argument list. The supported specifiers are:

.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a string.
.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints an integer.
.TP
.B %%
Prints the percentage sign '%'.

If an unsupported format specifier is encountered, _printf prints the '%' character followed by the unknown specifier.

.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
.I format
A constant character pointer representing the format string.

.TP
.I ...
Variable number of arguments to be formatted and printed according to the format string.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the total number of characters printed (excluding the null byte '\0'). If an error occurs, such as passing a NULL format string, the function returns -1.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B Example 1: Printing characters and strings
.nf
_printf("Hello %s!\n", "world");
Output: Hello world!
.fi

.B Example 2: Printing integers
.nf
_printf("Number: %d\n", 42);
Output: Number: 42
.fi

.B Example 3: Handling unsupported format specifiers
.nf
_printf("Value: %x\n", 255);
Output: Value: %x
.fi

.SH AUTHORS
William Lugo, Bryan Camacho, Eli Figueroa

.SH BUGS
Currently, this implementation does not support additional format specifiers such as %u, %o, %x, %X, or floating-point numbers.

If an unsupported specifier is encountered, it is printed as-is, prefixed with '%'.

	.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printf (3)
